Description: adapt the socket code to POSIX (no sin_len, no SO_NONBLOCK)
 V\OS follows the POSIX/Linux socket API: struct sockaddr_in has no
 sin_len member (that is a legacy BSD field), and setsockopt has no
 SO_NONBLOCK option (legacy systems carried it; POSIX flips a socket
 with fcntl(O_NONBLOCK) instead). Drop the two sin_len assignments and
 rewrite the blocking-mode switches with fcntl, keeping the original
 semantics (wouldBlock = true selects the blocking mode).
Author: VitruvianOS Packagers <maintainers@v-os.dev>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/FtpPositive
--- a/src/FTPClient.cpp
+++ b/src/FTPClient.cpp
